{"name": "R3F2_green_white_layout", "author": "Claude Opus 5.5", "notes": "1x1 conv: channel 0 = g-(r+b)/2 + 1 (always positive, so effectively linear; this completes the RGB thumbnail with R1F1); channel 1 = relu(r+g+b-2.4), the near-white fraction. Then avgpool16 gives a 4x4 grid, channel-major, rows top to bottom.", "layers": [{"type": "conv2d", "padding": 0, "weights": [[[[-0.5]], [[1]], [[-0.5]]], [[[1]], [[1]], [[1]]]], "bias": [1, -2.4], "names": ["green_excess_plus1", "white_frac"]}, {"type": "relu"}, {"type": "avgpool", "size": 16}, {"type": "flatten"}], "neurons": ["green+1 r0c0", "green+1 r0c1", "green+1 r0c2", "green+1 r0c3", "green+1 r1c0", "green+1 r1c1", "green+1 r1c2", "green+1 r1c3", "green+1 r2c0", "green+1 r2c1", "green+1 r2c2", "green+1 r2c3", "green+1 r3c0 grass", "green+1 r3c1 grass", "green+1 r3c2 grass", "green+1 r3c3 grass", "white r0c0", "white r0c1", "white r0c2", "white r0c3", "white r1c0", "white r1c1 ball/object", "white r1c2 ball/object", "white r1c3", "white r2c0", "white r2c1 ball/object", "white r2c2 ball/object", "white r2c3", "white r3c0", "white r3c1", "white r3c2", "white r3c3"]}